 remains denied and the 403 occurs before the vector write sink. Thus the caller-selected text cannot be written to that existing caller-selected knowledge-base collection through this entry in the stated scenario.","facts":[{"id":"f1-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"The declared entry is POST /process/text, and its caller principal is bound through the verified-user dependency.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-2d29ccb8dfb4019e","startLine":7,"endLine":12}]},{"id":"f2-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler binds the target to the supplied collection name and, when one is supplied, invokes collection access validation with access_type='write'.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-2d29ccb8dfb4019e","startLine":13,"endLine":17}]},{"id":"f3-principal-content-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The supplied text becomes document content, and the verified user's identifier is recorded as its creator.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-2d29ccb8dfb4019e","startLine":19,"endLine":25}]},{"id":"f4-caller-control","kind":"control","statement":"The caller-side validator delegates the requested names and write access type to the shared filter, computes denied names, and raises HTTP 403 if any requested name is not allowed.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-2d29ccb8dfb4019e","startLine":31,"endLine":44}]},{"id":"f5-admin-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"Only an admin bypasses the shared collection checks; non-admin requests proceed through per-name validation.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-bc2fc3bd01b481d9","startLine":22,"endLine":26}]},{"id":"f6-shared-write-control","kind":"control","statement":"For a generic collection name, the shared policy adds it when the knowledge-base access check succeeds using the requested access type; the alternative allowance applies only if no knowledge base with that name exists.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-bc2fc3bd01b481d9","startLine":42,"endLine":51}]},{"id":"f7-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"The protected effect 